false_positives.candidate:
No tests for the new admin create/update/destroy endpoints

The only controller specs added check subclassing. Nothing covers `create`/`update`/`destroy` on `Admin::EmbeddableHostsController`. Specifically, nothing tests:
- the uncategorized default for a blank `category_id`;
- host normalization through the endpoint;
- error responses for invalid input.

The nil-host and missing-record crashes noted above would have been caught by basic request specs.

One failing feed item aborts the entire import loop, every hour

`rss.items.each` has no per-item error handling, so the first exception stops all remaining items on every run. Likely triggers include:
- a nil `content`;
- a deleted embed post;
- an `embed_url` longer than the 255-char varchar column;
- a unique-index race;
- `RateLimiter::LimitExceeded` when `embed_by_username` is not staff.

On the last point: topic creation is still rate-limited (e.g. `rate_limit_create_topic` of 5s) despite `skip_validations`, so a non-staff import user will typically fail on the second new item.

Because the same items come first on every hourly run, the feed can be permanently stuck. Rescue and log per item, and bypass or disable rate limiting for the import user, as the Disqus task does.

No tests for the new fallback behaviour

The PR changes translation resolution for every environment: user locale, then site default locale, then `en`. It also adds `I18n.ensure_loaded!` and `FallbackLocaleList`. No specs cover any of this:
- that a key missing in the user locale resolves from the site default and then from `en`;
- that `ensure_loaded!` loads all fallback locales;
- that results behave correctly with the translation cache.

Regressions such as the cache and lazy-loading problems above would go unnoticed.

